<p dir=3D"ltr">In this case, you can also use =C2=ABcu=C2=BB. But you can&#=
39;t drop both.</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr">&gt;<br>
&gt; i le mlatu poi xekri vau kuho cu sipna vau<br>
&gt; The black cat sleeps.</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr">This example would be =C2=ABle mlatu poi xekri cu sipna=C2=
=BB.</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr">&gt;<br>
&gt; The &quot;le mlatu&quot; needs a &quot;ku&quot; that can go in one of =
two places, before or after the relative clause.</p>
<p dir=3D"ltr">Relative clauses follow the LE-clause, so =C2=ABku=C2=BB is =
